  </notes>
  <model id="pathway_9613354" metaid="metaid_0" name="Lipophagy">
    <notes>
      <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Triglycerides stored in lipid droplets are hydrolysed under nutrient starvation to release fatty acids for energy. The content of lipid droplets may vary but they are all coated with a protective protein called perilipin. When this protein is degraded, lipid droplets associate with autophagic components and breakdown into fatty acids (Ward C et al. 2016, Schulze R J et al. 2017). This process is termed as lipophagy (Singh R et al. 2009).</p>
    </notes>
